A retraction drops a parcel held whole for want of memory as if all of
its nodes were live in the version it falls back to. The ones the dead
segment created are reached by nothing and are never freed.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: a parcel held whole is freed in part when the head above it is retracted"

